Q: How do I programmatically handle swipe-to-scroll behavior? A: <p>I have resolved the issue after some testing and minor code modifications. I found that I need to adjust the sensitivity specifically for the swipe-to-scroll functionality (i.e., the <code>touchmove</code> event), as the desktop scrolling behavior is working correctly. Here's my working minor code modification:</p>
<pre><code>container.on(&quot;touchmove&quot;, function (e) {
  if (container.parent().is(&quot;.not-scrollable&quot;)) {
    return true;
  }

  const touchEndY = e.originalEvent.touches[0].clientY;
  const deltaMovingY = getMaxScrollY() &gt; 200 ? 10 : 100;
  const deltaY = touchStartY - touchEndY; // Determine swipe direction

  // Sensitivity control (lower = smoother)
  const scrollSpeed = 0.1; // adjust as necessary 

  if (deltaY &gt; 0) {
    move($(`#${scroll_thumb_id}`)[0], 0, deltaMovingY * scrollSpeed); // Scroll down
  } else {
    move($(`#${scroll_thumb_id}`)[0], 0, -deltaMovingY * scrollSpeed); // Scroll up
  }

  touchStartY = touchEndY; // Update for smooth scrolling

  e.preventDefault(); // Prevent default scrolling
});
</code></pre>
<p>This change makes the mobile and tablet swipe-to-scroll behavior smoother and slower, as desired.</p>

Q: Typescript + Svelte - How to add types to spread component props A: <p>You can use $$props variable of svelte.</p>
<p>app.svelte</p>
<pre><code>&lt;script&gt;
    import AgeInput from './AgeInput.svelte'
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;AgeInput 
    bi_p1=&quot;base input prop 1&quot; 
    bi_p2=&quot;base input prop 2&quot; 
    ai_p1=&quot;age input prop 1&quot; 
    ai_p2=&quot;age input prop 2&quot; 
/&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>baseinput.svelte</p>
<pre><code>&lt;script lang=&quot;ts&quot;&gt;
    export let bi_p1;
    export let bi_p2;
  // + a lot more props
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;input /&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;
    base input properties
    bi_p1: {bi_p1}
    bi_p2: {bi_p2}
&lt;/pre&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>ageinput.svelte</p>
<pre><code>&lt;script lang=&quot;ts&quot;&gt;
  import BaseInput from './BaseInput.svelte';

    const {bi_p1, bi_p2, ai_p1, ai_p2, ...restProps} = $$props
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;BaseInput {bi_p1} {bi_p2} type=&quot;number&quot; /&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;
    age input props
    ai_p1: {ai_p1}
    ai_p2: {ai_p2}
&lt;/pre&gt;
</code></pre>
